d6f8bd2a (686 1793272646172 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f360") (src . "daemon: refuse a public name spelled like another endpoint's lock\n\nAn endpoint X keeps two lock files beside its public name: its lifetime\nlock .X.lock and its reservation lock X.d.reserve. A public name spelled\nlike either is that file for X: serving at .s.lock or at s.d.reserve\nwhile s was not running made the name a publication link, and a later\nstart of s opened its own lock through it onto the socket and failed with\na refusal that named its own lock, not the endpoint that held the name.\nThe daemon's start now refuses such a name first, before it makes or\nlocks anything, with serve-name-derived naming the name, the endpoint it\nbelongs to and which lock it is, and exits 1 (a retry does not clear\nit). The test follows the socket directory's case rule and folds when the\nrule is not known. The other derived names are already safe: a public\nname spelled like X's namespace link is refused by occupancy whichever\nstart comes second, and one spelled like a backing directory is stepped\naround when X allocates its next one.\n\n- client.sc: lock-spelling, the shared test.\n- daemon.sc: the start's first clause; report-and-exit! takes the code.\n- README: the namespace paragraph says so.\n- Tests: daemon-namespace (the two lock shapes, case folding, ten other\n  names that serve, the refusal end to end, a plain name);\n  unreadable-census; rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 509))))
